### What variant of Codex are you using?

App

### What feature would you like to see?

Currently, the Codex App UI is entirely hardcoded. Users cannot extend the graphical interface to map their frequent local workflows. For instance, if I want a quick-access button in the status bar (bottom-right corner) to perform a local action (e.g., launching an external tool, triggering a custom deploy script, or opening a specific path), there is no way to achieve this.

I would like Codex App to support user-defined custom UI elements in the status bar or toolbars, similar to how the [vscode-commandbar](https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=gsppvo.vscode-commandbar) extension works in Visual Studio Code.It would be amazing if users could define a simple configuration file (e.g., .codex/commandbar.json or within config.toml) to inject custom buttons into the UI

```
{
  "commands": [
    {
      "text": "Unit Test",
      "command": "npm run test"
    },
    {
      "text": "Deploy",
      "command": "bash ./scripts/deploy.sh"
    },
  ]
}

```
